  "name": "Upper Goms valley, Valais, Switzerland",
  "summary": "Glacial valley floor of the upper Rhone at about 1340 m, between forested slopes rising to summits above 3000 m. The simulation's pad centre is placed on a hay meadow of the valley floor south of the river, read from the 2023 SWISSIMAGE orthophoto and chosen on the swissALTI3D model as the flattest open spot nearby, about 250 m from the end of a former airfield runway. The slopes rise within a kilometre; the relief figures give the departure from flat ground.",
