  "accuracy": [
    "Copernicus GLO-30 is a surface model: heights include buildings and vegetation canopy. Its stated absolute vertical accuracy is better than 4 m (90 % linear error); it does not resolve pads, roads or ground conditions.",
    "The 10 m image does not resolve structures; it is context only.",
    "The simulation assumes flat ground at z = 0 and computes no interaction with this terrain. Where the terrain rises above z = 0 the drawn trajectory may pass through it; this is a property of the geographic placement, not of the simulated flight.",
    "Horizontal registration of image and terrain follows the sources' georeferencing; Sentinel-2 L2A geolocation is of the order of 10 m.",
    "Detail layer (2.048 km square around the origin): heights from swissALTI3D 2024 bare-earth elevation model, 2 m tiles, heights in LN02 (EPSG:5728), sampled every 4 m and converted from EPSG:2056+5728 to EPSG:4937 ellipsoidal heights with PROJ (Inverse of Swiss Oblique Mercator 1995 + CH1903+ to ETRS89 (1) + Inverse of ETRS89 to LN02 height (with axis order normalized for visualization)); those are used as WGS84 heights. The origin is on this surface.",
    "swissALTI3D is a bare-earth model; its stated accuracy is in the swisstopo product documentation and was not checked against this pack. Buildings and forest are not in it, so the drawn terrain is the ground under them.",
    "Detail image: SWISSIMAGE 10 cm orthophoto mosaic, 2023 tiles (1 km cloud-optimised GeoTIFFs, 0.1 m) at 0.5 m per texel (source 0.1 m), resampled onto the ENU grid.",
    "swisstopo data are on CH1903+/LV95 (ETRS89-based); read here as WGS84 they are offset by of the order of 1 m on the ground. In steep terrain an orthophoto's residual relief displacement can reach a few metres.",
    "Within 192 m of the edge of the detail layer the drawn heights blend into the base grid and the detail image fades into the base image; this display adjustment is the only change made to the context data."
  ],
